node.doctext:
hello guys!<BR><BR>
I have a hash of hashes, for example:<CODE>
%hash = {
         abc => {
                 def => 1,
                },
         ghi => {
                 jkl => 1,
                },
};
</CODE>
What happen if I do:<CODE>
delete($hash{abc}{def});
</CODE>
am I staying with?:<CODE>
%hash = {
         abc => undef,
         ghi => {
                 jkl => 1,
                 mno => 1,
                },
};
</CODE>
That was the first question.<BR>
My second one is, I'm looping over the hash and delete keys as shown above if fulfilled a condition. If the ansewer to the first question is yes, is there a short way to delete also the first level key ('abc' in the example) when deleted all second level keys under it. In the example, when performing the above <I>delete</I>, i would have like to stay with:?:<CODE>
%hash = {
         ghi => {
                 jkl => 1,
                 mno => 1,
                },
};
</CODE>
Thanks
